The only permitted historical/current divergence is `products/rea-studio/server.mjs`, old7741-byte SHA `807a473ec0334f60dfd58f2df8901c722f1bd4eb1d64c62d9ba1ea65c2b6b55f` to new7840-byte SHA `85fe09b1b52a1d91e9d09c85d99c6e768ac4b793f5d7694a1760a4c0560a0a94`. Root51's strict public aliases are `products/rea-studio/results/sketch-layout-reviewed-installation-20261013/shared-route/frozen/{originalPath}.snapshot`, with exact manifest SHA `86de6ef0f1f39a03d7c6b4039cbbc78d0230c0ab09aec6ea61aa105edaedb3f9`. The proposal authenticates every51 payload and the manifest, strict52-file tree, exact runtime metadata, and the single99-byte staticMap insertion. It hashes the route proof's new bytes and current host, removes that one line, and compares the inverse byte-for-byte to the old host obtained from the immutable3ba capsule (manifest SHA `d969655ed6d1e73f925147c277261b38333e2d095b18a486f2c7c2a7700689ff`). The browser's different private7853-byte host is never substituted here.

