At old line70, the unchanged6745-byte Editor Save child (SHA `4b93961b46b79fe901eafcfc3e1eda564803b60a12be411feb58350da604f001`) runs without `--require-current`. Its default observed output schema is `rea-editor-save-public-followup-verification/v1`; it passes historical174 objects/516 records/current78 proof authentication while honestly reporting `liveSourceMatch:false`, `requireCurrent:false`, and exactly one mismatch `{path,testedSha256,liveSha256}` for the pinned host. Mismatch rows do not include byte lengths, so the parent separately authenticates both lengths. The proposal asserts this exact singleton, schema/passed/source count/zero behavior fields and checks current host again after the child. It preserves the child's false live-match report rather than rebinding the historical proof or fabricating all-current equivalence. An explicit `editorHostTransition` return field explains the narrow exception.

One default child metadata run exited0. One proposed-parent standalone metadata process also exited0 with all narrow checks. The run uses a separate execution adapter: only the two metadata dependency imports are retargeted to their unchanged root file URLs and the standalone root argument is set explicitly. Proposal semantics and published root source remain untouched. Both proposed and execution-adapter syntax checks pass. Raw output and before/after source hashes are retained. App tests, original helpers/programs, browsers, hosts, benchmarks and fullsuite executions are zero; this is proof/source verification, not current host behavior acceptance. Root's actual current Sketch39/HTTP2 evidence remains a separate forthcoming epoch.

The first wrapper expected one JSON document in stdout. Importing the Notes metadata verifier under `--standalone` emits its own JSON record before the parent result, so the parent stdout has two JSON lines. Parent exit0 and all raw output were already preserved; wrapper exit1 after `JSON.parse` was a collector parsing-premise failure. The exact wrapper and error are retained in `failures/`. A reparse-only step authenticates both lines and extracts the last explicit parent record; it reruns no parent/application/original code. Harmless initial metadata reads of absent guessed filenames are preparation diagnostics only.

This proposal checks immutable evidence and the exact current host byte transition; it does not prove endpoint behavior, continuous filesystem monitoring, atomic installation, broad product parity, resource isolation or security equivalence. Root should check the original parent hash, apply the six source transformations, then append other integration changes in their own source epoch. Historical Editor Save78 proof, child verifier and old3ba snapshot identities remain unchanged.
